      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "DATABASE",
      "narration_text": "For the backend, we are planning PostgreSQL to organize projects, videos, frames, labels, and annotations. Because location matters for conservation, PostGIS can provide a proper home for geographic information and spatial queries.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeScienceLayerStack",
          "props": {
            "sparkLine": "Store the observation where it happened.",
            "layers": [
              {
                "title": "PostgreSQL",
                "sub": "projects · videos · frames"
              },
              {
                "title": "PostGIS",
                "sub": "locations and spatial queries",
                "accent": true
              },
              {
                "title": "Annotation",
                "sub": "label connected to its source"
              }
            ],
            "caption": "The database preserves both the record and its geography."
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 16.55,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-09-01T18:49:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "QUESTIONS",
      "narration_text": "Once those pieces are connected, researchers can ask better questions: where were loons detected, which areas had the most observations, and how did observations change between captures? Over time, those records may also be compared with habitat changes.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeScienceChipGrid",
          "props": {
            "sparkLine": "Context turns detections into questions.",
            "items": [
              "Where were loons detected?",
              "Which areas had most observations?",
              "What changed between captures?",
              "How does habitat change relate?"
            ],
            "cols": 2,
            "caption": "Spatial and temporal questions become queryable."
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 16.45,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-09-01T18:49:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "MEANING",
      "narration_text": "This metadata pipeline is not just database housekeeping. It connects an AI detection back to the real world. The goal is not simply to say, that is a loon. It is to say, a loon was detected here, at this time, in this footage, at this location.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeScienceLayerStack",
          "props": {
            "sparkLine": "From prediction to field evidence.",
            "layers": [
              {
                "title": "AI detection",
                "sub": "a model finds a possible loon"
              },
              {
                "title": "Metadata context",
                "sub": "time · place · footage",
                "accent": true
              },
              {
                "title": "Conservation observation",
                "sub": "a result researchers can interpret"
              }
            ],
            "caption": "The real-world context is part of the result."
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 16.09,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-09-01T18:49:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "VERDICT",
      "narration_text": "The annotation system gives researchers a label, and the metadata pipeline gives that label context. Together they connect raw footage to a time-stamped, located observation. That is the foundation for building a useful machine learning dataset.",
